  "methodology": "cross_instance_parallel_clone",
  "methodology_note": "c9gd.8xlarge (ARM Graviton5) and c8id.8xlarge (Intel x86_64), 32 vCPU / 64 GiB / local NVMe instance store, the newest available class per architecture (Graviton5 against 8th-generation Intel); 5 fresh fastVEP clones and 1 Ensembl VEP clone per architecture, each booting the stock base image and syncing the dataset to local NVMe, then running scripts/concordance/run_clone_measurement.sh --walltime-only --engine <engine> on the cells: one cold-cache warmup, discarded and its output deleted, then one timed run per cell; fastVEP at 16 threads and Ensembl VEP at --fork 16 on sites-only inputs. Median and P5/P95 across the clones per cell (Weibull, R type 6); below 20 clones the P5 and P95 are the cell's minimum and maximum.",
